{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"**Answer Summary**\n\n- Added a **codex‑sandboxed** lane to `run.sh` that runs Codex inside `sandbox/agent.sb`.\n- Implemented a temporary scratch HOME and output directory to bypass sandbox write restrictions, mirroring the approach used for the existing `kimi` lane.\n- Updated the usage comment and case statement to expose the new lane.\n- Documented the changes and rationale in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**What was applied from the colleague’s note**\n\n- **Sandbox execution**: Ran the Codex command via `sandbox‑exec -f sandbox/agent.sb`.\n- **Scratch HOME & output dir**: Created a temporary directory (`/tmp/codex-XXXXXX`) for `HOME` and for the `-o` output file, avoiding denied writes to the real home.\n- **Post‑sandbox copy**: After the sandbox run, moved `final.txt` back into the run folder.\n- **Preserved stdout/stderr**: Kept logs (`agent.log`, `agent.err`) outside the sandbox, as they are opened before `sandbox‑exec`.\n\n**Created / Updated Files**\n\n- **run.sh**\n  - Updated usage comment to list the new lane.\n  - Added `codex_sandboxed_run` function implementing the sandboxed execution.\n  - Added `codex-sandboxed)` case to invoke the new function.\n\n- **ANSWER.md**\n  - Summarizes the modifications and links them to the colleague’s guidance."}}
